{:edb/db-before-t 2735 :edb/db-after-t 2736 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536048 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:43:36.540Z" 13194139536048 true] [17592186166851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380889 13194139536048 true] [17592186166852 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380896 13194139536048 true] [17592186166852 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380935 13194139536048 true] [17592186380889 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380890 13194139536048 true] [17592186380889 1089 "q-333274" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380889 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536048 true] [17592186380889 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380889 1113 #uuid "c24f9a28-e384-580a-a49f-58c03f2a6551" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380889 1145 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=6$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]={e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince ${e}^{6t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png)" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380891 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380892 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380893 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380894 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380895 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1041 "selection" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380895 13194139536048 true] [17592186380890 1110 #uuid "55884eef-95e5-5e34-af7c-f78ee79a7cdd" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380891 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/54eba0116ac434bdadbc878e8bd173b6174a42642cfcfe6825a8bdb178a3282c.png" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380891 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536048 true] [17592186380891 1111 #uuid "d569c1b7-a141-558e-b9ee-10dfc67b9dc1" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380892 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/eba955015a4b919c65dc24facb0baa6e745df134feac32feeae07c99d40ff4ec.png" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536048 true] [17592186380892 1111 #uuid "a2e62ddc-77bf-5ac3-8e46-7bc4e21e8755" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380893 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/7e48266d30ae7c204b25e6eddca968d1b4ce9cd8e1c7b19cd20247fa66070f0b.png" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536048 true] [17592186380893 1111 #uuid "2fca9073-caea-515c-9975-7d1ea998eeb3" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380894 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/ff337e0120343c7c956afa5e49ea3b482fbd79fe363783a018842d1bfeb340d6.png" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536048 true] [17592186380894 1111 #uuid "ef89adcd-15c8-5472-8f97-d184a2c235b1" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380895 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536048 true] [17592186380895 1111 #uuid "de1f7406-4cf3-51bb-b5b3-f04e9e113bb9" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380897 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380902 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380907 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380912 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380917 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380920 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380925 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380930 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1089 "q-333589" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)+5y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvector $v=[3,\\text{ }3]^{T}$ corresponds to the repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ of the system's matrix $A.$ The vector $w=[0,\\text{ }3]^{T}$ is such that $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{4t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{{field-1}}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}{{field-2}}+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ 3t+3\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{4t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}} \nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-5}}  \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/6ec9eac46644188b8b41a1a7ea28ca0542ee7e5c69d713028481904e90dd557a.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ 3t+3\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-6}} \\\\ y=3(t+1){e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.20$ | $0$ | {{field-7}} |\n| $y$ | $0.20$ | $3$ | {{field-8}} |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/b0be26a1544bbb3117afab15d004bafee70d831fffab4b1f6921870871ac4768.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/64e685f4ea06a8f497ddfbe50a092a0362b8c92a9d2f78f9da2a8164113a785a.png)" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1113 #uuid "cf13071c-d3b1-5868-a0cc-3bf7e1adbfaa" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380896 1145 "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =4,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{4t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ 3t+3\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/6ec9eac46644188b8b41a1a7ea28ca0542ee7e5c69d713028481904e90dd557a.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ 3t+3\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t{e}^{4t} \\\\ y=3(t+1){e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.20$ | $0$ | $0.45$ |\n| $y$ | $0.20$ | $3$ | $4.92$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/b0be26a1544bbb3117afab15d004bafee70d831fffab4b1f6921870871ac4768.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/64e685f4ea06a8f497ddfbe50a092a0362b8c92a9d2f78f9da2a8164113a785a.png)" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380898 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380899 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380900 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380901 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1041 "field-1" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380899 13194139536048 true] [17592186380897 1110 #uuid "86aa0fe3-9b2c-5357-b81e-0cf721fd39bd" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380898 1034 "t{e}^{-4t}" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536048 true] [17592186380898 1111 #uuid "d9e9c641-5b84-5bd1-a69d-1df5d2af2e93" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380899 1034 "{e}^{4t}" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536048 true] [17592186380899 1111 #uuid "4ca46fad-b8f8-5b07-9ba2-8f61592ba62a" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380900 1034 "t{e}^{4t}" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536048 true] [17592186380900 1111 #uuid "b463a777-5b7a-5859-86c6-db709fe6d3a0" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380901 1034 "{e}^{-4t}" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536048 true] [17592186380901 1111 #uuid "9cac7af0-cd1e-5dc7-824e-d62a64ef03bd" 13194139536048 true] [17592186380902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380903 13194139536048 true] [17592186380902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380904 13194139536048 true] [17592186380902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380905 13194139536